comments.content:
The coalescing loop is buggy. When `drop` becomes true, the code shifts subsequent entries down by one (`option_callbacks[i] = option_callbacks[i + 1]`) but `num_option_callbacks` is never decremented, so the last (now duplicated) slot still gets iterated in `mp_option_run_callbacks`, executing a stale callback twice.

Also, when multiple entries match, only the first match triggers `drop` and then *every* remaining entry gets shifted regardless of whether it matches — this corrupts the queue and can drop unrelated pending callbacks. Consider finding the matching index, removing that single entry via MP_TARRAY_REMOVE_AT (which decrements the count), then appending the new one. For example:

    bool drop = false;
    for (int i = 0; i < mpctx->num_option_callbacks; i++) {
        struct mp_option_callback *cb = &mpctx->option_callbacks[i];
        if ((flags && flags == cb->flags) ||
            (cb->co && opt_ptr == cb->co->data)) {
            MP_TARRAY_REMOVE_AT(mpctx->option_callbacks,
                                mpctx->num_option_callbacks, i);
            drop = true;
            break;
        }
    }

Then always append the new callback (the coalescing just removed the older duplicate).

